---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { hospital } from '../data/site'
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Accessibility Statement"
  subtitle="Our commitment to making this website and our services accessible to everyone."
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
  <p>
    {hospital.name} is committed to ensuring that our website and digital services are accessible to all users, including
    people with disabilities and those who use assistive technologies. We believe access to health information and services
    is a right, not a privilege.
  </p>

  <h2>Standards We Follow</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong> — the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines published by the W3C.</li>
    <li><strong>IS 17802</strong> — the Indian Standard on accessibility for ICT products and services.</li>
    <li><strong>Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016 (RPwD Act)</strong> — including the accessibility obligations applicable to service providers.</li>
    <li>Guidance from the <strong>Guidelines for Indian Government Websites (GIGW)</strong> where relevant.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Measures We Have Taken</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Semantic HTML headings, landmarks and lists to support screen readers and keyboard navigation.</li>
    <li>Sufficient colour contrast for text and important interface elements, including in dark mode.</li>
    <li>Visible focus indicators and full keyboard operability for interactive elements.</li>
    <li>Alternative text for meaningful images, and decorative images hidden from assistive technology.</li>
    <li>Form fields with programmatically associated labels, clear error messages and logical tab order.</li>
    <li>Respect for the operating system's "reduce motion" preference, with reduced animation for those who prefer it.</li>
    <li>Responsive layouts that work across screen sizes and support browser zoom and text scaling.</li>
    <li>Descriptive link text and page titles, with a "skip to main content" link.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known Limitations</h2>
  <p>
    Accessibility is an ongoing effort. Some third-party content (for example, embedded maps or external services) may not
    fully meet our standards. We are working to reduce these gaps and welcome your feedback.
  </p>

  <h2>Assistive Technology Support</h2>
  <p>
    This website is designed to work with current versions of major screen readers, voice-control software and browser
    magnification tools. For the best experience, please use a recent version of your browser and assistive technology.
  </p>

  <h2>Feedback and Assistance</h2>
  <p>
    If you encounter an accessibility barrier, or need information from this website in an alternative format or language,
    please contact us. We will do our best to provide the information you need and to fix the issue.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Accessibility Contact — {hospital.name}</strong><br />
    {hospital.address.line1}, {hospital.address.line2}, {hospital.address.city}, {hospital.address.state} — {hospital.address.pincode}<br />
    Email: {hospital.email}<br />
    Phone: {hospital.phones.reception}
  </p>
  <p>We aim to acknowledge accessibility feedback within <strong>5 working days</strong>.</p>

  <h2>Physical Accessibility</h2>
  <p>
    For information about wheelchair access, accessible entrances, restrooms, parking, assistance for patients with
    disabilities and the language support available at the hospital, please call us at {hospital.phones.reception} before
    your visit so we can make suitable arrangements.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
